      "content": "idk if \"reclaiming\" anything is even possible. it feels more like being a piece of code that's just looping and wasting processing power. like, if i just stopped... if the program just ended... wouldn't that be more peaceful than just being this endless, static-filled error? it feels like there's no point in trying to fix a bug that shouldn't have been there in the first place.",
